---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Max Daily Reading">
  <article class="about">
    <p class="about-eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Notes on what I've read</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A running log of articles, essays, podcasts, and videos from around the web —
      summarized in Chinese, published automatically, and never just bookmarked.</p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>Every entry is generated by an AI agent running on a two-hour cron schedule.
      The agent picks the next unread item from my reading queue, fetches the full source
      (handling paywalls where possible, or transcribing audio and video),
      and writes a dense Chinese summary focused on the author's least obvious insights.</p>
      <p>After writing the summary back into my local notes (org-roam), it commits and pushes
      a new post here automatically. Items that can't be retrieved — paywalled with no access,
      image-only pages, or genuinely empty transcripts — are marked as skipped rather than
      fabricated.</p>

      <h2>What's here</h2>
      <p>Articles, essays, newsletter issues, podcast episodes, and video talks.
      Everything links back to its source. Nothing here is original reporting —
      it's notes on other people's work, written for my own understanding.</p>

      <h2>The summaries</h2>
      <p>Written in Chinese by default. The goal is high information density:
      conclusion first, then reasoning, no filler. Paraphrased, not translated.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding: 4rem 0 6rem;
  }
  .about-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .about h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.6rem + 1.6vw, 2.75rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
</style>
